14635012	Association of TNF - beta polymorphism with disease severity among patients infected with hepatitis C virus .|The pathogenesis of chronic hepatitis C virus ( HCV ) infection remains unclear .|Tumour necrosis factor alpha ( TNF - alpha ) is alleged to contribute in the pathogenesis of chronic HCV infection .|Single nucleotide polymorphism in TNF - alpha and - beta genes could influence the outcome of HCV infection .|The aim was to study single nucleotide polymorphism in TNF - alpha promoter region and Nco I polymorphisms in the TNF - beta gene in patients with chronic hepatitis C .|Fifty - two patients with histologically proven chronic hepatitis , who had raised ALT levels ( > 1 . 5 x ULN ) and were HCV RNA positive , were studied .|Genotyping of - 308 promoter variant of TNF - alpha was performed by PCR with primers that incorporated an Nco I restriction site .|For PCR typing of the TNF - beta Nco I restriction fragment length polymorphism , sequence specific primers were used .|Polymorphism in the TNF - alpha G / G , G / A and A / A allele was not different between HCV patients and healthy controls .|TNF - beta A / A allele was significantly more common ( P = 0 . 02 ) in patients ( 28 . 8 % ) as compared to controls ( 12 . 8 % ) , whereas no significant difference was observed for TNF - beta G / A and G / G alleles [ corrected ] .|Nco I TNF - beta A / A was strongly associated with - 308 TNF - alpha G / G ( RR of HCV persistence = 4 . 9 ) , indicating possible linkage between TNF - beta A / A and TNF - alpha G / G allele .|Patients with severe hepatic fibrosis more frequently had the TNF - beta A / A allele as compared to patients with mild disease ( P = 0 . 04 ) .|Immunogenetic factors , such as single nucleotide polymorphisms in TNF - beta ( A / A allele ) , may affect the natural course of HCV infection , in particular , the disease progression .|Larger studies including cytokine expression profiles are needed to fully understand the contribution of the polymorphisms described in the pathogenesis of chronic hepatitis C .	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	11-16	2-5	4049	TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta	Gene	2:91:163:207:268:301:325:356	5:94:166:210:271:304:328:359	0:4:7:9:10:10:11:12	D006526	infected with hepatitis C virus|chronic hepatitis C virus ( HCV ) infection|HCV infection|HCV infection|HCV infection	Disease	11:20:49:68:372	16:28:51:70:374	0:1:2:3:12	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	56-59	49-51	7124	TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - beta G / A and G|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha	Gene	36:56:80:141:182:251:280:308	39:59:83:144:185:259:283:311	2:3:4:6:8:9:10:10	D006526	infected with hepatitis C virus|chronic hepatitis C virus ( HCV ) infection|HCV infection|HCV infection|HCV infection	Disease	11:20:49:68:372	16:28:51:70:374	0:1:2:3:12	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	325-328	319-321	4049	TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta	Gene	2:91:163:207:268:301:325:356	5:94:166:210:271:304:328:359	0:4:7:9:10:10:11:12	D008103	hepatic fibrosis	Disease	319	321	11	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	319-321	308-311	7124	TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - beta G / A and G|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha	Gene	36:56:80:141:182:251:280:308	39:59:83:144:185:259:283:311	2:3:4:6:8:9:10:10	D008103	hepatic fibrosis	Disease	319	321	11	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	31-33	2-5	4049	TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta	Gene	2:91:163:207:268:301:325:356	5:94:166:210:271:304:328:359	0:4:7:9:10:10:11:12	D009369	Tumour necrosis	Disease	31	33	2	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	36-39	31-33	7124	TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - beta G / A and G|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha	Gene	36:56:80:141:182:251:280:308	39:59:83:144:185:259:283:311	2:3:4:6:8:9:10:10	D009369	Tumour necrosis	Disease	31	33	2	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	98-101	91-94	4049	TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|TNF - beta|