15377847	Genetic variants of the sulfotransferase 1A1 and breast cancer risk .|Sulfotransferase 1A1 ( SULT1A1 ) , also designated as phenol - preferring sulfotransferase , is involved in the bioactivation and detoxification of a variety of potential carcinogens , including iodothyronines , hydroxylated aromatic amines , and phenolic xenobiotics .|A common arginine ( R ) to histidine ( H ) polymorphism at amino acid position 213 influences SULT1A1 activity and has been suggested as risk factor for a different types of cancers .|To investigate the role of this polymorphism for breast cancer risk , SULT1A1 genotype was determined in 500 women with clinically verified breast cancer and 500 female age - matched healthy control subjects .|Frequencies of heterozygous ( controls : 42 . 5 % patients : 50 . 2 % ) or homozygous ( controls : 12 . 6 % ; patients : 9 . 4 % ) carriers of the 213H variant were not significantly different between groups .|The SULT1A1 genotype was furthermore not associated with tumor size , histological grading , estrogen or progesterone receptor status and age at diagnosis .|The SULT1A1 213H variant was associated with the presence of lymph node metastases ( p = 0 . 002 ) .|We conclude that the SULT1A1 R213H polymorphism is not a general risk factor for breast cancer , but may be involved in lymph node metastazing in breast cancer patients .	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	223-225	180-182	5241	progesterone receptor	Gene	180	182	5	D001943	breast cancer|breast cancer|breast cancer|breast cancer|breast cancer	Disease	7:92:106:223:235	9:94:108:225:237	0:3:3:7:7	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	11-13	7-9	6817	sulfotransferase 1A1|Sulfotransferase 1A1|SULT1A1|SULT1A1|SULT1A1|SULT1A1|SULT1A1|SULT1A1	Gene	4:11:14:68:96:165:189:213	6:13:15:69:97:166:190:214	0:1:1:2:3:5:6:7	D001943	breast cancer|breast cancer|breast cancer|breast cancer|breast cancer	Disease	7:92:106:223:235	9:94:108:225:237	0:3:3:7:7	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	200-201	180-182	5241	progesterone receptor	Gene	180	182	5	D009362	