15515206	Identification of a dysferlin gene mutation in a Korean case with Miyoshi myopathy .|Recent genetic and immunohistochemical analyses have shown that Miyoshi myopathy ( MM ) is caused by a mutation in the DYSF gene , which induces dysfunction of dysferlin .|The author described one patient showing characteristic MM phenotype with deficiency of dysferlin on immunohistochemistry .|Direct DNA sequencing of whole exons of DYSF gene revealed one homozygous missense mutation ( G1165C ) on exon 12 , which let to an amino acid substitution from the glutamic acid to glutamine at the 389 of the peptide sequence in this patient .|This is the first reported case of MM confirmed by immunohistochemical and genetic analyses in Korea .	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	55-56	50-51	8291	dysferlin|DYSF|dysferlin|dysferlin|DYSF	Gene	3:34:41:55:66	4:35:42:56:67	0:1:1:2:3	C537480	Miyoshi myopathy|Miyoshi myopathy|MM|MM|MM	Disease	11:22:25:50:111	13:24:26:51:112	0:1:1:2:4	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	55-56	53-56	8291	dysferlin|DYSF|dysferlin|dysferlin|DYSF	Gene	3:34:41:55:66	4:35:42:56:67	0:1:1:2:3	D003677	deficiency of dysferlin	Disease	53	56	2
