16225776	Association of HLA - DQ with idiopathic dilated cardiomyopathy in a northern Chinese Han population .|Autoimmune mechanisms are likely involved in the pathogenesis of idiopathic dilated cardiomyopathy ( IDC ) and components of MHC may serve as markers for the propensity to develop immune - mediated myocardial damage .|This study was conducted to investigate the possible association between HLA - DQA1 , - DQB1 alleles and IDC in Han population from northern China by using PCR - based sequence - specific primer ( PCR - SSP ) technique for HLA genotyping .|Among 68 unrelated IDC patients , 4 probands of IDC pedigrees and 100 healthy controls , we found that the alleles of HLA - DQA1 * 0501 and HLA - DQB1 * 0303 conferred susceptibility to IDC while HLA - DQA1 * 0201 and HLA - DQB1 * 0502 , * 0504 alleles were in negative association with IDC .|The serine at position 57 ( SER57 ) in the exon of HLA - DQB1 * 0502 and * 0504 was confirmed in our experiment as a marker for resistance to IDC .|The results suggest that HLA - DQ polymorphism may be involved in the pathogenesis of IDC .	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	132-135	130-131	3117	HLA - DQA1|HLA - DQA1|HLA - DQA1	Gene	60:116:132	63:119:135	2:3:3	C536277	idiopathic dilated cardiomyopathy|idiopathic dilated cardiomyopathy|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC	Disease	6:25:29:68:97:103:130:152:185:202	9:28:30:69:98:104:131:153:186:203	0:1:1:2:3:3:3:3:4:5	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	68-69	65-66	3119	DQB1|HLA - DQB1|HLA - DQB1|HLA - DQB1	Gene	65:122:138:166	66:125:141:169	2:3:3:4	C536277	idiopathic dilated cardiomyopathy|idiopathic dilated cardiomyopathy|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC	Disease	6:25:29:68:97:103:130:152:185:202	9:28:30:69:98:104:131:153:186:203	0:1:1:2:3:3:3:3:4:5	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	34-35	29-30	3133	MHC	Gene	34	35	1	C536277	idiopathic dilated cardiomyopathy|idiopathic dilated cardiomyopathy|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC|IDC	Disease	6:25:29:68:97:103:130:152:185:202	9:28:30:69:98:104:131:153:186:203	0:1:1:2:3:3:3:3:4:5	1:GD