17548676	Association of polymorphisms in one - carbon metabolism genes and postmenopausal breast cancer incidence .|The interconversion of folates by the one - carbon metabolism pathway is essential for the synthesis of precursors used in DNA synthesis , repair , and methylation .|Perturbations in this pathway can disrupt these processes and are hypothesized to facilitate carcinogenesis .|We investigated associations of 25 candidate polymorphisms in nine one - carbon metabolism genes with risk of postmenopausal breast cancer using 502 cases and 505 controls from the Cancer Prevention II Nutrition Cohort .|Four single nucleotide polymorphisms ( SNP ) in three different genes were significantly associated with breast cancer .|The nonsynonymous R134K SNP in methylenetetrahydrofolate dehydrogenase / methenyltetrahydrofolate cyclohydrolase / formyltetrahydrofolate synthase [ MTHFD1 ; odds ratio ( OR ) , 1 . 40 ; 95 % confidence interval ( 95 % CI ) , 1 . 06 - 1 . 85 for CT + TT ] and an intronic SNP in formyltetrahydrofolate dehydrogenase ( FTHFD ; OR , 2 . 23 ; 95 % CI , 1 . 09 - 4 . 54 for CC ) were associated with a significant increase in risk .|Significantly decreased risk was associated with an intronic SNP in FTHFD ( OR , 0 . 75 ; 95 % CI , 0 . 58 - 0 . 98 for CT + CC ) and the A360A SNP in cystathionine beta - synthase ( CBS ; OR , 0 . 63 ; 95 % CI , 0 . 41 - 0 . 96 for TT ) .|The presence of at least one variant from both the methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase ( MTHFR ) C677T and A1298C SNPs was also associated with increased risk ( OR , 2 . 16 ; 95 % CI , 1 . 34 - 3 . 48 for 677 CT + TT / 1 , 298 AC + CC ) .|Investigations into interactions of the associated SNPs with each other and with dietary factors yielded inconclusive results .|Our findings indicate that genetic variation in multiple one - carbon metabolism genes may influence risk of postmenopausal breast cancer and may involve changes in methyl donor synthesis .|However , larger studies are needed to further examine gene / gene and gene / diet interactions in this pathway .	1:GDA:2	R2L	CROSS	163-165	107-109	10840	formyltetrahydrofolate dehydrogenase|FTHFD|FTHFD	Gene	163:166:207	165:167:208	5:5:6	D001943	postmenopausal breast cancer|postmenopausal breast cancer|breast cancer|postmenopausal breast cancer	Disease	10:75:107:356	13:78:109:359	0:3:4:9	1:GDA:2	R2L	CROSS	124-125	107-109	4522	MTHFD1	Gene	124	125	5	D001943	postmenopausal breast cancer|postmenopausal breast cancer|breast cancer|postmenopausal breast cancer	Disease	10:75:107:356	13:78:109:359	0:3:4:9	1:GDA:2	R2L	CROSS	356-359	277-278	4524	methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase|MTHFR	Gene	274:277	276:278	7:7	D001943	postmenopausal breast cancer|postmenopausal breast cancer|breast cancer|postmenopausal breast cancer	Disease	10:75:107:356	13:78:109:359	0:3:4:9	1:GDA:2	R2L	CROSS	356-359	236-240	875	cystathionine beta - synthase	Gene	236	240	6	D001943	postmenopausal breast cancer|postmenopausal breast cancer|breast cancer|postmenopausal breast cancer	Disease	10:75:107:356	13:78:109:359	0:3:4:9	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	163-165	86-87	10840	formyltetrahydrofolate dehydrogenase|FTHFD|FTHFD	Gene	163:166:207	165:167:208	5:5:6	D009369	Cancer	Disease	86	87	3	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	124-125	86-87	4522	MTHFD1	Gene	124	125	5	D009369	Cancer	Disease	86	87	3	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	274-276	86-87	4524	methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase|MTHFR	Gene	274:277	276:278	7:7	D009369	Cancer	Disease	86	87	3	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	236-240	86-87	875	cystathionine beta - synthase	Gene	236	240	6	D009369	Cancer	Disease	86	87	3	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	163-165	56-57	10840	formyltetrahydrofolate dehydrogenase|FTHFD|FTHFD	Gene	163:166:207	165:167:208	5:5:6	D063646	carcinogenesis	Disease	56	57	2	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	124-125	56-57	4522	MTHFD1	Gene	124	125	5	D063646	carcinogenesis	Disease	56	57	2	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	274-276	56-57	4524	methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase|MTHFR	Gene	274:277	276:278	7:7	D063646	carcinogenesis	Disease	56	57	2	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	236-240	56-57	875	cystathionine beta -