17646849	CNTNAP2 gene dosage variation is associated with schizophrenia and epilepsy .|A homozygous mutation of the CNTNAP2 gene has been associated with a syndrome of focal epilepsy , mental retardation , language regression and other neuropsychiatric problems in children of the Old Order Amish community .|Here we report genomic rearrangements resulting in haploinsufficiency of the CNTNAP2 gene in association with epilepsy and schizophrenia .|Genomic deletions of varying sizes affecting the CNTNAP2 gene were identified in three non - related Caucasian patients .|In contrast , we did not observe any dosage variation for this gene in 512 healthy controls .|Moreover , this genomic region has not been identified as showing large - scale copy number variation .|Our data thus confirm an association of CNTNAP2 to epilepsy outside the Old Order Amish population and suggest that dosage alteration of this gene may lead to a complex phenotype of schizophrenia , epilepsy and cognitive impairment .	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	35-37	16-17	26047	CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2	Gene	0:16:56:72:127	1:17:57:73:128	0:1:2:3:6	D001523	neuropsychiatric problems	Disease	35	37	1	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	155-157	127-128	26047	CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2	Gene	0:16:56:72:127	1:17:57:73:128	0:1:2:3:6	D003072	cognitive impairment	Disease	155	157	6	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	129-130	127-128	26047	CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2	Gene	0:16:56:72:127	1:17:57:73:128	0:1:2:3:6	D004827	epilepsy|epilepsy|epilepsy|epilepsy	Disease	9:61:129:153	10:62:130:154	0:2:6:6	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	25-27	16-17	26047	CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2	Gene	0:16:56:72:127	1:17:57:73:128	0:1:2:3:6	D004828	focal epilepsy	Disease	25	27	1	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	28-30	16-17	26047	CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2	Gene	0:16:56:72:127	1:17:57:73:128	0:1:2:3:6	D008607	mental retardation	Disease	28	30	1	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	7-8	0-1	26047	CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2|CNTNAP2	Gene	0:16:56:72:127	1:17:57