18285833	IFIH1 - GCA - KCNH7 locus : influence on multiple sclerosis risk .|A recent genome - wide scan of nonsynonymous SNPs and ulterior validation in case - control and family analyses evidenced a susceptibility locus for type 1 diabetes ( T1D ) on chromosome 2q24 . 3 .|We aimed at testing the effect of this locus in other autoimmune diseases with complex genetic background , such as multiple sclerosis ( MS ) .|Four SNPs along the locus , rs13422767 , rs2111485 , rs1990760 and rs2068330 , were genotyped using TaqMan MGB chemistry in 311 T1D and 412 MS patients and 535 ethnically matched healthy controls .|The previously reported association of this locus was found for the first time in MS ( rs2068330 , G vs C : P = 0 . 001 ; OR ( 95 % CI ) = 0 . 73 ( 0 . 6 - 0 . 88 ) ) and a trend for replication was observed in our Spanish diabetic cohort .|Therefore , genes included in this locus - IFIH1 interferon induced helicase , GCA grancalcin or the potassium channel KCNH7 - are potential candidates implicated in the pathogenesis of these autoimmune diseases , although strong linkage disequilibrium in the region hampered further localization of the etiologic gene .	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	200-202	184-185	25801	grancalcin	Gene	184	185	5	D001327	autoimmune diseases|autoimmune diseases	Disease	60:200	62:202	2:5	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	200-202	178-179	64135	IFIH1|IFIH1	Gene	0:178	1:179	0:5	D001327	autoimmune diseases|autoimmune diseases	Disease	60:200	62:202	2:5	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	200-202	189-190	90134	KCNH7|KCNH7	Gene	4:189	5:190	0:5	D001327	autoimmune diseases|autoimmune diseases	Disease	60:200	62:202	2:5	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	184-185	167-168	25801	grancalcin	Gene	184	185	5	D003920	diabetic	Disease	167	168	4	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	178-179	167-168	64135	IFIH1|IFIH1	Gene	0:178	1:179	0:5	D003920	diabetic	Disease	167	168	4	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	189-190	167-168	90134	KCNH7|KCNH7	Gene	4:189	5:190	0:5	D003920	diabetic	Disease	167	168	4	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	184-185	97-98	25801	grancalcin	Gene	184	185	5	D0