18615679	Novel V600E BRAF mutations in imatinib - naive and imatinib - resistant gastrointestinal stromal tumors .|BRAF and NRAS are commonly mutated in cancer and represent the most frequent genetic events in malignant melanoma .|More recently , a subset of melanomas was shown to overexpress KIT and harbor KIT mutations .|Although most gastrointestinal stromal tumors ( GISTs ) exhibit activating mutations in either KIT or PDGFRA , about 10 % of the cases lack mutations in these genes .|It is our hypothesis following the melanoma model that mutations in BRAF or NRAS may play a role in wild - type GIST pathogenesis .|Alterations in RAS / MEK / ERK pathway may also be involved in development of imatinib resistance in GIST , particularly in tumors lacking secondary KIT or PDGFRA mutations .|Imatinib - naive wild - type GISTs from 61 patients , including 15 children and 28 imatinib - resistant tumors without secondary KIT mutations were analyzed .|Screening for hot spots mutations in BRAF ( exons 11 and 15 ) and NRAS ( exons 2 and 3 ) was performed .|A BRAF exon 15 V600E was identified in 3 of 61 GIST patients , who shared similar clinical features , being 49 - to 55 - years - old females and having their tumors located in the small bowel .|The tumors were strongly KIT immunoreactive and had a high risk of malignancy .|An identical V600E BRAF mutation was also identified in one of 28 imatinib resistant GIST lacking a defined mechanism of drug resistance .|In conclusion , we identified a primary BRAF V600E mutations in 7 % of adult GIST patients , lacking KIT / PDGFRA mutations .|The BRAF - mutated GISTs show predilection for small bowel location and high risk of malignancy .|A secondary V600E BRAF mutation could represent an alternative mechanism of imatinib resistance .|Kinase inhibitors targeting BRAF may be effective therapeutic options in this molecular GIST subset .	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	103-104	94-95	4893	NRAS|NRAS|NRAS	Gene	18:94:177	19:95:178	1:4:7	C564650	GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST	Disease	103:124:198:255:279:331	104:125:199:256:280:332	4:5:8:10:11:14	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	285-286	279-280	5156	PDGFRA|PDGFRA|PDGFRA	Gene	67:133:285	68:134:286	3:5:11	C564650	GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST	Disease	103:124:198:255:279:331	104:125:199:256:280:332	4:5:8:10:11:14	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	112-113	103-104	5594	ERK	Gene	112	113	5	C564650	GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST	Disease	103:124:198:255:279:331	104:125:199:256:280:332	4:5:8:10:11:14	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	110-111	103-104	5609	MEK	Gene	110	111	5	C564650	GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST	Disease	103:124:198:255:279:331	104:125:199:256:280:332	4:5:8:10:11:14	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	279-280	271-272	673	BRAF|BRAF|BRAF|BRAF|BRAF|BRAF|BRAF|BRAF|BRAF|BRAF	Gene	2:16:92:169:188:244:271:289:308:322	3:17:93:170:189:245:272:290:309:323	0:1:4:7:8:10:11:12:13:14	C564650	GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST|GIST	Disease	103:124:198:255:279:331	104:125:199:256:280:332	4:5:8:10:11:14	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	94-95	87-88	4893	NRAS|NRAS|NRAS	Gene	18:94:177	19:95:178	1:4:7	D008545	malignant melanoma|melanomas|melanoma	Disease	32:41:87	34:42:88	1:2:4	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	87-88	67-68	5156	PDGFRA|PDGFRA|PDGFRA	Gene	67:133:285	68:134:286	3:5:11	D008545	malignant melanoma|melanomas|melanoma	Disease	32:41:87	34:42:88	1:2:4	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	112-113	87-88	5594	ERK	Gene	112	113	5	D008545	malignant melanoma|melanomas|melanoma	Disease	32:41:87	34:42:88	1:2:4	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	110-111	87-88	5609	MEK	Gene	110	111	5	D008545	malignant melanoma|melanomas|melanoma	Disease	32:41:87	34:42:88	1:2:4	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	92-93	87-88	673	BRAF|BRAF|BRAF|BRAF|BRAF|BRAF|BRAF|BRAF|BRAF|BRAF	Gene	2:16:92:169:188:244:271:289:308:322	3:17:93:170:189:245:272:290:309:323	0:1:4:7:8:10:11:12:13:14	D008545	malignant melanoma|melanomas|melanoma	Disease	32:41:87	34:42:88	1:2:4	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	23-24	18-19	4893	NRAS|NRAS|NRAS	Gene	18:94:177	19:95:178	1:4:7	D009369	cancer|tumors|tumors|tumors|tumors|malignancy|malignancy	Disease	23:128:155:220:228:239:303	24:129:156: