19741716	Association of copy number variation in the FCGR3B gene with risk of autoimmune diseases .|Copy number variation ( CNV ) in the human genome is an important determinant of susceptibility to autoimmune diseases .|Many autoimmune diseases share similar clinical and pathogenic features .|Thus , CNVs of genes involved in immunity may serve as shared determinants of multiple autoimmune diseases .|Here , we determined the association between CNV in the gene encoding FCGR3B with the risk of developing autoimmune diseases and whether the observed associations are modified by the CNV in CCL3L1 ( CC chemokine ligand 3 - like 1 ) , a gene encoding a potent chemokine .|In a cross - sectional study of 774 subjects , we estimated FCGR3B and CCL3L1 gene copy number in 146 , 158 and 61 subjects with systemic lupus erythematosus ( SLE ) , rheumatoid arthritis ( RA ) and primary Sj gren 's syndrome ( SS ) , respectively , and 409 healthy controls .|The median gene dose of FCGR3B in the study population was two .|FCGR3B copy number < or > 2 was associated with an increased risk of SLE and primary SS but not RA .|This association was mostly evident in subjects who also had two copies of CCL3L1 .|Thus , our data suggest that epistatic interactions between CNV of FCGR3B and CCL3L1 , two immune response genes , may influence phenotypically related autoimmune diseases .	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	200-201	180-181	2215	FCGR3B|FCGR3B|FCGR3B|FCGR3B|FCGR3B|FCGR3B	Gene	7:75:124:172:180:228	8:76:125:173:181:229	0:4:5:6:7:9	D001172	rheumatoid arthritis|RA|RA	Disease	145:148:200	147:149:201	5:5:7	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	215-216	200-201	6349	CCL3L1|CCL3L1|CCL3L1|CCL3L1	Gene	94:126:215:230	95:127:216:231	4:5:8:9	D001172	rheumatoid arthritis|RA|RA	Disease	145:148:200	147:149:201	5:5:7	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	12-14	7-8	2215	FCGR3B|FCGR3B|FCGR3B|FCGR3B|FCGR3B|FCGR3B	Gene	7:75:124:172:180:228	8:76:125:173:181:229	0:4:5:6:7:9	D001327	autoimmune diseases|autoimmune diseases|autoimmune diseases|autoimmune dis