19800079	Association of polymorphisms of the tryptophan hydroxylase 2 gene with risk for bipolar disorder or suicidal behavior .|Bipolar disorder ( BD ) is a severe psychiatric illness characterized by the occurrence of elevated mood alternating with depressive episodes , having a estimated lifetime prevalence of 0 . 4 - 1 . 6 % using DSM - IV criteria .|Disturbances of the central serotonergic system has been associated with the pathophysiology of affective disorders and suicidal behavior .|Tryptophan hydroxylase 2 ( TPH2 ) which is a rate limiting enzyme in the serotonin synthesis is considered an important candidate gene associated with psychiatric disorders .|Our sample consisted of 527 subjects ( 303 diagnosed with bipolar disorder and 224 healthy controls ) which were genotyped for eight tagSNPs ( rs4448731 , rs4565946 , rs11179000 , rs7955501 , rs10506645 , rs4760820 , rs1487275 and rs10879357 ) covering the whole gene of the human TPH2 .|Statistical analyses were performed using UNPHASED version 3 . 0 . 12 and Haploview ( ( R ) ) .|Single markers , genotype and haplotype association analysis did not show significant genetic association with bipolar disorder or suicidal behavior .|Our findings do not support the association between diagnosis of BD or suicidal behavior and TPH2 polymorphisms .	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	103-105	83-84	121278	tryptophan hydroxylase 2|Tryptophan hydroxylase 2|TPH2|TPH2|TPH2	Gene	5:79:83:153:211	8:82:84:154:212	0:3:3:4:7	D001523	psychiatric illness|psychiatric disorders	Disease	26:103	28:105	1:3	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	211-212	206-207	121278	tryptophan hydroxylase 2|Tryptophan hydroxylase 2|TPH2|TPH2|TPH2	Gene	5:79:83:153:211	8:82:84:154:212	0:3:3:4:7	D001714	bipolar disorder|Bipolar disorder|BD|bipolar disorder|bipolar disorder|BD	Disease	12:18:21:116:190:206	14:20:22:118:192:207	0:1:1:4:6:7	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	37-38	5-8	121278	tryptophan hydroxylase 2|Tryptophan hydroxylase 2|TPH2|TPH2|TPH2	Gene	5:79:83:153:211	8:82:84:154:212	0:3:3:4:7	D0