20006695	Expression of prestin and Gata - 3 , - 2 , - 1 mRNA in the rat organ of Corti during the postnatal period and in culture .|Based on observations that mutations of GATA - 3 are responsible for the HDR - syndrome ( hypoparathyroidism , deafness , renal defects ) and that GATA - transcription factors have an important role to play in inner ear development , we hypothesized that these transcription factors may be involved in regulatory changes of prestin transcription .|To prove this , we examined in parallel the expression of mRNA of prestin and Gata - 3 , - 2 and Gata - 1 in the organ of Corti during early postnatal development of rats and in organotypic cultures .|Remarkable relations are observed between prestin and Gata - 3 , - 2 expression in organ of Corti preparations in vivo and in vitro : ( i ) Gata - 3 , - 2 expression display similar apical - basal gradients as prestin mRNA levels .|( ii ) The prestin expression increases between postnatal day two and postnatal day eight by a factor of about four in the apical and middle segments and by a factor of two in the basal part .|Highly significant Pearson correlation coefficients were observed between Gata - 3 , - 2 mRNA and prestin levels when the data were evaluated by regression analyses .|( iii ) Parallel changes of prestin mRNA and Gata - 3 , - 2 mRNA levels were observed in response to thyroid hormone and to gemfibrozil application .|These observations suggest a regulatory role played by the Gata - 3 , - 2 transcription factors in prestin expression .	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	107-110	41-44	2623	Gata - 1	Gene	107	110	2	C537907	HDR - syndrome	Disease	41	44	1	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	100-106	41-44	2624	Gata - 3 , - 2|Gata - 3 , - 2|Gata - 3 , - 2|Gata - 3 , - 2|Gata - 3 , - 2	Gene	100:154:218:246:275	106:160:224:252:281	2:3:5:6:7	C537907	HDR - syndrome	Disease	41	44	1	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	41-44	34-37	2625	Gata - 3 , - 2|Gata - 3 , - 2|Gata - 3 , - 2|Gata - 3 , - 2|Gata - 3 , - 2|Gata - 3|GATA - 3|Gata - 3	Gene	100:154