20515557	Prevalence and prognostic significance of FLT3 gene mutations in patients with acute leukaemia : analysis of patients from the Shanghai Leukaemia Co - operative Group .|This study was designed to evaluate the prevalence of fms - like tyrosine kinase - 3 ( FLT3 ) gene mutations in the World Health Organization classified subtypes of acute leukaemia ( AL ) , and their prognostic significance in terms of complete remission ( CR ) , leukaemia - free survival ( LFS ) and overall survival ( OS ) .|Of 468 patients , 374 ( 79 . 9 % ) had acute myeloid leukaemia ( AML ) and 83 ( 17 . 7 % ) had acute lymphoblastic leukaemia ( ALL ) .|Among the AML patients , a FLT3 internal tandem duplication ( FLT3 / ITD ) mutation was present in 59 cases ( 15 . 8 % ) , whereas a FLT3 / D835 mutation was detected in 15 cases ( 4 . 0 % ) .|Conversely , in the ALL patients , no FLT3 / ITD mutations were detected and a FLT3 / D835 mutation was found in only two cases ( 2 . 4 % ) .|The FLT3 / ITD mutation was associated with a lower CR rate compared with those with no mutations ( 52 . 3 % versus 71 . 1 % ) and with a shorter median OS ( 9 versus 18 months ) in AML patients .|In conclusion , the FLT3 / ITD mutation occurred frequently in AML and was associated with a lower CR and shorter median OS .|In contrast , FLT3 / D835 mutations were not of prognostic value .	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	11-13	5-6	2322	FLT3|fms - like tyrosine kinase - 3|FLT3|FLT3|FLT3|FLT3|FLT3|FLT3|FLT3|FLT3|FLT3	Gene	5:35:43:128:133:152:176:184:202:250:273	6:42:44:129:134:153:177:185:203:251:274	0:1:1:3:3:3:4:4:5:6:7	D007938	acute leukaemia|Leukaemia|acute leukaemia|AL|leukaemia	Disease	11:20:55:58:74	13:21:57:59:75	0:0:1:1:1	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	128-129	124-125	2322	FLT3|fms - like tyrosine kinase - 3|FLT3|FLT3|FLT3|FLT3|FLT3|FLT3|FLT3|FLT3|FLT3	Gene	5:35:43:128:133:152:176:184:202:250:273	6:42:44:129:134:153:177:185:203:251:274	0:1:1:3:3:3:4:4:5:6:7	D015470	acute myeloid leukaemia|AML|AML|AML|AML	Disease	100:104:124: