22684020	Regulatory role of KEAP1 and NRF2 in PPARy expression and chemoresistance in human non - small - cell lung carcinoma cells .|The nuclear factor - E2 - related factor 2 ( NRF2 ) serves as a master regulator in cellular defense against oxidative stress and chemical detoxification .|However , persistent activation of NRF2 resulting from mutations in NRF2 and / or downregulation of or mutations in its suppressor , Kelch - like ECH - associated protein 1 ( KEAP1 ) , is associated with tumorigenicity and chemoresistance of non - small - cell lung carcinomas ( NSCLCs ) .|Thus , inhibiting the NRF2 - mediated adaptive antioxidant response is widely considered a promising strategy to prevent tumor growth and reverse chemoresistance in NSCLCs .|Unexpectedly , stable knockdown of KEAP1 by lentiviral shRNA sensitized three independent NSCLC cell lines ( A549 , HTB - 178 , and HTB - 182 ) to multiple chemotherapeutic agents , including arsenic trioxide ( As ( 2 ) O ( 3 ) ) , etoposide , and doxorubicin , despite moderately increased NRF2 levels .|In lung adenocarcinoma epithelial A549 cells , silencing of KEAP1 augmented the expression of peroxisome proliferator - activated receptor y ( PPARy ) and genes associated with cell differentiation , including E - cadherin and gelsolin .|In addition , KEAP1 - knockdown A549 cells displayed attenuated expression of the proto - oncogene cyclin D1 and markers for cancer stem cells ( CSCs ) and reduced nonadherent sphere formation .|Moreover , deficiency of KEAP1 led to elevated induction of PPARy in response to As ( 2 ) O ( 3 ) .|Pretreatment of A549 cells with PPARy agonists activated PPARy and augmented the cytotoxicity of As ( 2 ) O ( 3 ) .|A mathematical model was formulated to advance a hypothesis that differential regulation of PPARy and detoxification enzymes by KEAP1 and NRF2 may underpin the observed landscape changes in chemosensitivity .|Collectively , suppression of KEAP1 expression in human NSCLC cells resulted in sensitization to chemotherapeutic agents , which may be attributed to activation of PPARy and subsequent alterations in cell differentiation and CSC abundance .	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	219-220	125-126	2934	gelsolin	Gene	219	220	5	D002289	non - small - cell lung carcinoma|non - small - cell lung carcinomas|NSCLCs|NSCLCs	Disease	13:90:98:125	20:97:99:126	0:2:2:3	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	23-31	13-20	4780	NRF2|nuclear factor - E2 - related factor 2|NRF2|NRF2|NRF2|NRF2|NRF2|NRF2	Gene	5:23:32:54:59:105:181:320	6:31:33:55:60:106:182:321	0:1:1:2:2:3:4:9	D002289	non - small - cell lung carcinoma|non - small - cell lung carcinomas|NSCLCs|NSCLCs	Disease	13:90:98:125	20:97:99:126	0:2:2:3	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	13-20	7-8	5468	PPARy|peroxisome proliferator - activated receptor y|PPARy|PPARy|PPARy|PPARy|PPARy|PPARy	Gene	7:198:205:264:282:285:313:354	8:204:206:265:283:286:314:355	0:5:5:7:8:8:9:10	D002289	non - small - cell lung carcinoma|non - small - cell lung carcinomas|NSCLCs|NSCLCs	Disease	13:90:98:125	20:97:99:126	0:2:2:3	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	237-239	125-126	595	cyclin D1	Gene	237	239	6	D002289	non - small - cell lung carcinoma|non - small - cell lung carcinomas|NSCLCs|NSCLCs	Disease	13:90:98:125	20:97:99:126	0:2:2:3	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	132-133	125-126	9817	KEAP1|Kelch - like ECH - associated protein 1|KEAP1|KEAP1|KEAP1|KEAP1|KEAP1|KEAP1|KEAP1	Gene	3:71:80:132:193:224:258:318:334	4:79:81:133:194:225:259:319:335	0:2:2:4:5:6:7:9:10	D002289	non - small - cell lung carcinoma|non - small - cell lung carcinomas|NSCLCs|NSCLCs	Disease	13:90:98:125	20:97:99:126	0:2:2:3	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	215-218	125-126	999	E - cadherin	Gene	215	218	5	D002289	non - small - cell lung carcinoma|non - small - cell lung carcinomas|NSCLCs|NSCLCs	Disease	13:90:98:125	20:97:99:126	0:2:2:3	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	219-220	86-87	2934	gelsolin	Gene	219	220	5	D002471	tumorigenicity	Disease	86	87	2	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	105-106	86-87	4780	NRF2|nuclear factor - E2 - related factor 2|NRF2|NRF2|NRF2|NRF2|NRF2|NRF2	Gene	5:23:32:54:59:105:181:320