23104008	Bayesian refinement of association signals for 14 loci in 3 common diseases .|To further investigate susceptibility loci identified by genome - wide association studies , we genotyped 5 , 500 SNPs across 14 associated regions in 8 , 000 samples from a control group and 3 diseases : type 2 diabetes ( T2D ) , coronary artery disease ( CAD ) and Graves ' disease .|We defined , using Bayes theorem , credible sets of SNPs that were 95 % likely , based on posterior probability , to contain the causal disease - associated SNPs .|In 3 of the 14 regions , TCF7L2 ( T2D ) , CTLA4 ( Graves ' disease ) and CDKN2A - CDKN2B ( T2D ) , much of the posterior probability rested on a single SNP , and , in 4 other regions ( CDKN2A - CDKN2B ( CAD ) and CDKAL1 , FTO and HHEX ( T2D ) ) , the 95 % sets were small , thereby excluding most SNPs as potentially causal .|Very few SNPs in our credible sets had annotated functions , illustrating the limitations in understanding the mechanisms underlying susceptibility to common diseases .|Our results also show the value of more detailed mapping to target sequences for functional studies .	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	117-120	56-59	1029	CDKN2A - CDKN2B|CDKN2A	Gene	117:142	120:143	3:3	D003324	coronary artery disease	Disease	56	59	1	1:GDA:2	R2L	CROSS	117-120	56-59	1030	CDKN2A - CDKN2B|CDKN2B	Gene	117:144	120:145	3:3	D003324	coronary artery disease	Disease	56	59	1	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	110-111	56-59	1493	CTLA4	Gene	110	111	3	D003324	coronary artery disease	Disease	56	59	1	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	153-154	56-59	3087	HHEX	Gene	153	154	3	D003324	coronary artery disease	Disease	56	59	1	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	149-150	56-59	54901	CDKAL1	Gene	149	150	3	D003324	coronary artery disease	Disease	56	59	1	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	105-106	56-59	6934	TCF7L2	Gene	105	106	3	D003324	coronary artery disease	Disease	56	59	1	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	151-152	56-59	79068	FTO	Gene	151	152	3	D003324	coronary artery disease	Disease	56	59	1	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	121-122	117-120	1029	CDKN2A - CDKN2B|CDKN2A	Gene	117:1