7550232	Four novel mutations underlying mild or intermediate forms of alpha - L - iduronidase deficiency ( MPS IS and MPS IH / S ) .|The alpha - L - iduronidase deficiency diseases ( Mucopolysaccharidosis I ) cover a spectrum of clinical severity ranging from the very severe ( Hurler syndrome , MPS IH ) through an intermediate ( Hurler / Scheie syndrome , MPS IH / S ) to a relatively mild form ( Scheie syndrome , MPS IS ) .|Numerous mutations of the gene encoding alpha - L - iduronidase ( IDUA ) are known in Hurler syndrome , but only three in the other disorders .|We report on novel mutations of the IDUA gene in one patient with the Scheie syndrome and in three patients with the Hurler / Scheie syndrome .|The novel mutations , all single base changes , encoded the substitutions R492P ( Scheie ) , and X654G , P496L , and L490P ( Hurler / Scheie ) .|The L490P mutation was apparently homozygous , whereas each of the others was found in compound heterozygosity with a Hurler mutation .|The deleterious nature of the mutations was confirmed by absence of enzyme activity upon transfection of the corresponding mutagenized cDNAs into Cos - 1 cells .|These results provide additional information for genotype - phenotype correlations .	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	88-93	64-66	3425	alpha - L - iduronidase|IDUA|IDUA	Gene	88:94:117	93:95:118	2:2:3	C565524	MPS IH|MPS IH|MPS IH	Disease	19:52:64	21:54:66	0:1:1	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	99-101	94-95	3425	alpha - L - iduronidase|IDUA|IDUA	Gene	88:94:117	93:95:118	2:2:3	D008059	alpha - L - iduronidase deficiency|alpha - L - iduronidase deficiency|Mucopolysaccharidosis I|Hurler syndrome|Hurler / Scheie syndrome|Scheie syndrome|Hurler syndrome|Scheie syndrome|Hurler / Scheie syndrome	Disease	9:26:34:49:59:75:99:124:132	15:32:36:51:63:77:101:126:136	0:1:1:1:1:1:2:3:3
