8777952	Association between toluene diisocyanate - induced asthma and DQB1 markers : a possible role for aspartic acid at position 57 .|Toluene diisocyanate ( TDI ) is the most common cause of occupational asthma in western countries .|The aim of this study was to investigate whether genetic factors are involved in toluene diisocyanate - induced asthma .|We studied the frequency of human leucocyte antigen ( HLA ) class II genetic markers in three groups of subjects : 1 ) subjects with TDI - induced asthma ( n = 30 ) ; 2 ) exposed subjects with no history of TDI - induced asthma ( n = 12 ) ; and 3 ) normal subjects not exposed to TDI ( n = 126 ) .|Venous blood samples were collected from the three groups and the polymorphic second exon of DQA and DQB genes was amplified by the polymerase chain reaction ( PCR ) method .|Evaluation of HLA class II gene products in TDI - induced asthma cases showed a positive association with HLA - DQB1 * 0503 and a negative association with HLA - DQB1 * 0501 alleles , which differed at residue 57 for a single amino acid , i . e . aspartic acid in DQB1 * 0503 and valine in DQB1 * 0501 .|No significant difference was found in the distribution of DQA1 alleles between asthmatics and controls .|Our results confirm the hypothesis that HLA - DQB1 * 0503 has a role in conferring susceptibility to TDI - induced asthma and that residue 57 of HLA - DQB1 is a potentially critical location .	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	257-258	229-230	3117	DQA1	Gene	229	230	6	D001249	asthma|asthma|asthma|asthma|asthma|asthma	Disease	6:56:86:104:168:257	7:57:87:105:169:258	0:2:3:3:5:7	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	8-9	6-7	3119	DQB1|HLA - DQB1|HLA - DQB1|DQB1|DQB1|HLA - DQB1|HLA - DQB1	Gene	8:175:185:210:216:242:263	9:178:188:211:217:245:266	0:5:5:5:5:7:7	D001249	asthma|asthma|asthma|asthma|asthma|asthma	Disease	6:56:86:104:168:257	7:57:87:105:169:258	0:2:3:3:5:7	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	229-230	32-34	3117	DQA1	Gene	229	230	6	D059366	occupational asthma	Disease	32	34	1	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	32-34	8