9129974	Evaluation of TAP1 polymorphisms with insulin dependent diabetes mellitus in Finnish diabetic patients .|The Childhood Diabetes in Finland ( DiMe ) Study Group .|Insulin dependent diabetes mellitus ( IDDM ) is an autoimmune disease with a strong association between disease and the HLA class II region .|Because abnormal antigen processing , in part characterized by altered class I processing , has been identified in patients with IDDM , the TAP ( transporter associated with antigen processing ) genes located in the HLA class II region make attractive candidate genes for IDDM .|Five coding region variants of TAP1 were typed in a cohort of well characterized Finnish patients with diabetes ( n = 119 ) and compared to racially marched control subjects ( n = 92 ) .|We found that although no single TAP1 polymorphism was associated with IDDM , a genotypic combination of Ile / Val at codon 333 with Asp / Asp at codon 637 was found more frequently in subjects with IDDM ( 9 . 4 % ) compared to controls ( 1 . 2 % ; p = 0 . 025 ) .|This could not be accounted for by an association with any particular haplotype defined by class I or class II serology .	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	34-36	30-31	3630	IDDM|IDDM|IDDM|IDDM|IDDM	Gene	30:69:93:142:168	31:70:94:143:169	2:3:3:5:5	D001327	autoimmune disease	Disease	34	36	2	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	34-36	2-3	6890	TAP1|transporter associated with antigen processing|TAP1|TAP1	Gene	2:74:100:137	3:79:101:138	0:3:4:5	D001327	autoimmune disease	Disease	34	36	2	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	30-31	16-17	3630	IDDM|IDDM|IDDM|IDDM|IDDM	Gene	30:69:93:142:168	31:70:94:143:169	2:3:3:5:5	D003920	diabetic|Diabetes|diabetes	Disease	11:16:112	12:17:113	0:1:4	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	11-12	2-3	6890	TAP1|transporter associated with antigen processing|TAP1|TAP1	Gene	2:74:100:137	3:79:101:138	0:3:4:5	D003920	diabetic|Diabetes|diabetes	Disease	11:16:112	12:17:113	0:1:4	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	30-31	30-31	3630	IDDM|IDDM|IDDM|IDDM|IDDM	Gene	30:69:93:142:168	31:70:94:143:169	2:3:3:5:5	D003922	i