11289718	Correlation of genetic etiology with response to beta - adrenergic blockade among symptomatic patients with familial long - QT syndrome .|Mutations in any of the five genes KCNQ1 , KCNH2 , KCNE1 , KCNE2 , and SCN5A can be responsible for familial long QT syndrome ( LQTS ) , an arrhythmogenic disorder that entails a high risk of sudden death .|beta - Adrenergic blocking agents are the first therapeutic choice , and 80 % of patients treated with these agents show symptomatic relief ; however the remaining 20 % do not respond well .|We previously performed a nationwide analysis of familial long QT syndrome ( LQTS ) in Japan and identified 32 mutations in the KCNQ1 and KCNH2 genes .|In the present retrospective study , we found that patients carrying mutations in the KCNQ1 gene responded better to beta - adrenergic blocking agents than those with KCNH2 mutations ( 12 of 13 vs 1 of 5 ; P = 0 . 0077 , Fisher 's exact test ) .|This is a good example of the power of genetic diagnosis to direct the selection of appropriate therapy for patients with diseases of heterogeneous genetic etiology .	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	59-61	32-33	3753	KCNE1	Gene	32	33	1	D003645	sudden death	Disease	59	61	1	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	59-61	30-31	3757	KCNH2|KCNH2|KCNH2	Gene	30:120:150	31:121:151	1:3:4	D003645	sudden death	Disease	59	61	1	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	59-61	28-29	3784	KCNQ1|KCNQ1|KCNQ1	Gene	28:118:137	29:119:138	1:3:4	D003645	sudden death	Disease	59	61	1	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	59-61	37-38	6331	SCN5A	Gene	37	38	1	D003645	sudden death	Disease	59	61	1	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	59-61	34-35	9992	KCNE2	Gene	34	35	1	D003645	sudden death	Disease	59	61	1	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	42-46	32-33	3753	KCNE1	Gene	32	33	1	D008133	familial long - QT syndrome|familial long QT syndrome|familial long QT syndrome	Disease	15:42:103	20:46:107	0:1:3	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	30-31	15-20	3757	KCNH2|KCNH2|KCNH2	Gene	30:120:150	31:121:151	1:3:4	D008133	familial long - QT syndrome|familial long QT syndrome|familial long QT syndrom