11525424	Estrogen receptor alpha gene polymorphism in schizophrenia : frequency , age at onset , symptomatology and prognosis .|Schizophrenic disorders are equally distributed for both sexes ; however , later onset , milder psychopathology and better outcome are associated with the female gender .|This sex difference is thought to be partly due to the estrogen system .|Recent studies have determined that estrogen receptor alpha subtype ( ER alpha ) genetic polymorphisms may affect the expression of ER alpha , and are associated with Alzheimer 's disease .|For this study , we investigated the association of ER alpha polymorphisms for 125 schizophrenic patients and 142 control subjects .|No significant differences for genotype distribution or allele frequency were revealed comparing controls and schizophrenic patients .|The ER alpha genotypes were not associated with onset age , psychiatric symptoms or outcome for schizophrenic cases .|With new research highlighting the prominent role of sex hormones in neurological and psychological dysfunction , further study is needed to explore the genetic effect of the sex hormone receptor gene on susceptibility mental disorders and associations with different phenotypes .	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	85-88	78-80	2099	Estrogen receptor alpha|estrogen receptor alpha|ER alpha|ER alpha|ER alpha|ER alpha	Gene	0:63:68:78:98:128	3:66:70:80:100:130	0:3:3:3:4:6	D000544	Alzheimer 's disease	Disease	85	88	3	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	138-139	128-130	2099	Estrogen receptor alpha|estrogen receptor alpha|ER alpha|ER alpha|ER alpha|ER alpha	Gene	0:63:68:78:98:128	3:66:70:80:100:130	0:3:3:3:4:6	D001523	psychiatric	Disease	138	139	6	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	128-130	124-125	2099	Estrogen receptor alpha|estrogen receptor alpha|ER alpha|ER alpha|ER alpha|ER alpha	Gene	0:63:68:78:98:128	3:66:70:80:100:130	0:3:3:3:4:6	D012559	schizophrenia|Schizophrenic disorders|schizophrenic|schizophrenic|schizophrenic	Disease	6:18:103:124:143	7:20:104:125:144	0:1:4:5:6	1:NR:2	R2L	