18797455	GSTP1 Ile105Val polymorphism correlates with progression - free survival in MCRC patients treated with or without irinotecan : a study of the Dutch Colorectal Cancer Group .|A Valine residue at position 105 of the GSTP1 protein results in decreased enzyme activity .|As nuclear GSTP1 activity decreases irinotecan cytotoxicity , Val - allele carriers may benefit more from irinotecan chemotherapy .|Our aim was to investigate the association of GSTP1 genotype with treatment outcome of irinotecan .|Progression - free survival ( PFS ) and toxicity were determined in 267 metastatic colorectal cancer ( MCRC ) patients who were treated with first - line capecitabine ( CAP ) plus irinotecan ( CAPIRI ) , or CAP single agent in a prospective randomised phase III trial ( CAIRO ) .|GSTP1 genotype was determined by Pyrosequencing .|Patients receiving CAP showed a PFS of 6 . 6 ( Ile / Ile ) , 6 . 0 ( Ile / Val ) and 6 . 5 months ( Val / Val ) ; compared to 7 . 0 ( Ile / Ile ) , 8 . 8 ( Ile / Val ) and 9 . 2 months ( Val / Val ) with CAPIRI .|Median PFS was 2 . 7 months longer in Val - allele carriers treated with CAPIRI compared to CAP ( P = 0 . 005 ) .|Patients with the Ile / Ile genotype showed similar PFS with CAPIRI and CAP ( 7 . 0 compared to 6 . 6 months , P = 0 . 972 ) .|Toxicity did not differ significantly among genotypes .|GSTP1 codon 105 polymorphism may be predictive for the response to irinotecan - based chemotherapy in patients with MCRC , with the Val - allele being associated with a better outcome .|Ile / Ile genotype patients do not appear to benefit from the addition of irinotecan to CAP .	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	35-36	23-25	2950	GSTP1|GSTP1|GSTP1|GSTP1|GSTP1|GSTP1	Gene	0:35:45:70:130:271	1:36:46:71:131:272	0:1:2:3:5:10	D015179	Colorectal Cancer|colorectal cancer	Disease	23:92	25:94	0:4	1:NR:2	R2L	CROSS	271-272	263-264	2950	GSTP1|GSTP1|GSTP1|GSTP1|GSTP1|GSTP1	Gene	0:35:45:70:130:271	1:36:46:71:131:272	0:1:2:3:5:10	D064420	toxicity|Toxicity	Disease	86:263	87