8843235	Variation in the tumor necrosis factor - alpha gene promoter region may be associated with death from meningococcal disease .|Tumor necrosis factor - alpha ( TNF - alpha ) plays a central role in the pathophysiology of sepsis .|Levels of TNF - alpha are directly correlated with severity in meningococcal disease ( MD ) .|A polymorphism in the promoter region of the TNF - alpha gene is associated with differences in the secretion of TNF - alpha .|The TNF2 allele is associated with higher constitutive and inducible levels of TNF - alpha secretion than is the TNF1 allele .|To investigate whether possession of the TNF2 allele is associated with severity in MD , the frequency of TNF1 and TNF2 alleles in 98 children with MD was compared .|There were more deaths among children who had the TNF2 allele ( P = . 03 ; relative risk [ RR ] , 2 . 5 ; 95 % confidence interval [ CI ] , 1 . 1 - 5 . 7 ) than in those who did not .|There was also an increased risk of severe disease in children with the TNF2 allele ( P = . 02 ; RR , 1 . 6 ; 95 % CI , 1 . 1 - 2 . 3 ) .|Possession of the TNF2 allele predisposes to a worse outcome in children with meningococcal infection .	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	20-25	15-16	7124	tumor necrosis factor - alpha|Tumor necrosis factor - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha	Gene	3:20:26:42:65:77:93	8:25:29:45:68:80:96	0:1:1:2:3:3:4	D003643	death	Disease	15	16	0	1:GDA:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	20-25	17-19	7124	tumor necrosis factor - alpha|Tumor necrosis factor - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha	Gene	3:20:26:42:65:77:93	8:25:29:45:68:80:96	0:1:1:2:3:3:4	D008589	meningococcal disease|meningococcal disease|MD|MD|MD|meningococcal infection	Disease	17:51:54:116:129:236	19:53:55:117:130:238	0:2:2:5:5:8	1:NR:2	R2L	NON-CROSS	42-45	38-39	7124	tumor necrosis factor - alpha|Tumor necrosis factor - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha|TNF - alpha	Gene	3:20:26:42:65:77:93	8:25:29:45:68:80:96	0:1:1:2:3